AUDIO: 'If you check out some of the newer templates from Comfy UI, you\'ll see they\'re featuring new INT8 models. Why is this good? Well, because the quality can be better than the old FP8s, and you get a speed boost, which even works on'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'older cards, such as my 3090. Hello, and welcome to more Nerdy Rodent Geekery. Just in case you\'re not familiar with the channel, I use the Rodent method for workflows, which means low spaghetti,'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'colorful, modular named groups, making stuff much easier to understand and to update. If you\'re following this tutorial to make or update your own workflows, don\'t forget you can pause to take screenshots or rewatch bits at any'

[00:38] [scene:visual example]
VISUAL: AI-generated image of anthropomorphic rodents in various professions
AUDIO: 'time. Also, if you find these videos helpful, prefer tutorials from actual humans, or perhaps you just like all this workflow creation stuff done for you already, then you can support the'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'channel via the Patreon link in the video description. It\'s your support which lets me make even more workflows for you and to share these free tutorials with everyone. That freedom to choose is, of course, yours, and a huge'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'thank you to all supporters, because it\'s you that makes this possible. Yes, FP8 models are now old news. These are being replaced by INT8 convolutional rotation models, or ConvRot for short.'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Not sure I like that shortening, but anyway, as well as actually beating out the FP8 versions on quality, they\'re also faster, which sounds like a win-win'

