[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clean as the INT8 version. So, slower and not quite as good. It\'s a similar story with Kwen Image Edit. Again, this first one being an INT8 result. As we\'ve seen before in earlier videos, Kwen is'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very colorful. But, now let\'s check out the slower FP8 mixed version. As expected, this version is very similar, but take a look at the rodent text on the fire helmet. Looks like the INT8'

[02:22] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow overview, showing purple-grouped nodes for model loaders, creation options
AUDIO: 'version wins out again. Zed image this time, and you will also get a pretty similar version. The INT8 one here to start with, and I thought, "Okay, let\'s try it against the double-size model,'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the BF16." As you can see, even against this version, the previous INT8 image holds up very well, and it is, of course, roughly twice as fast to generate. Those images were all generated using the same workflow, which'

[02:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'handles the various models via those loaders at the start, the purple groups on the left there. So, you can easily switch between the INT8 and whatever other type of model you fancy. I will go into more workflow details later on in'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the video, but because I like switches to easily flip between models, the workflow featured in this video has a lot of them. Check out my previous video on the linear switch if you\'re looking for more information on that. But, this'

[03:14] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: "Load Images" section with nodes for image loading, resizing, OpenPose preprocessor, mask generation
AUDIO: 'time, I\'m not just using it for the refiner stage, but also for the main model loaders at the beginning. I\'ll show you a few examples first, and then go into the workflow details so you can'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create this workflow for yourself. But, to start with, I\'m using Kwen Image Edit because that\'s one of the few models that can give you things from poses or canny or depth images. In this case, I\'m'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'starting out with an image which is pre-processed into a pose, along with a simple prompt for a photorealistic image of a guy on the ground on a strange alien planet. This does give us the'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'posed result. However, one thing about Kwen image edit is that it doesn\'t do too well with photo realism and that\'s where the refiners come in. For refiner one, I\'ve chosen option C, which is Z'

[04:04] [scene:result]
VISUAL: AI-generated image of a man posing on an alien planet, demonstrating Qwen Image Edit's initial output
AUDIO: 'image and for refiner two, I went with option A, which is Korea two. In the first compare group, you can see the original Kwen image generation as mentioned, not very photo realistic.'

[04:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Very smooth and kind of oversaturated with those colors, but as I slide across, you can see the first refiner pass with Z image and it\'s almost like night and day. The weird kind of'

[04:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plasticky look gives way to something a lot more like a photo realistic style. In the second compare group, we can see what Korea two did, which is perhaps even more of a photo style. The plants,'

[04:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the lighting, the shadows are all a bit better, I think. Of course, this is just one example of the options you can use. You could use Korea two first and then Z image second if you like or two sets of'

[04:56] [scene:result]
VISUAL: AI-generated black and white comic art style image of a man, demonstrating Qwen Image Edit's output for specific styles
AUDIO: 'Z image. Kwen isn\'t always rubbish at styles though and as mentioned, it is one of the few models that can use poses or the other various control net pre processed images. This time I\'ve got a'

[05:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompt for a black and white gothic comic art style sketch depicting a man in a heatwave. This time the result is very much better. Now, the refiners don\'t have to do so much work to repair'

[05:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'things. Plus, you could simply upscale if you like this result, but just want a higher resolution. For a two times upscale, this Wyan VAE gives great results and very quickly, you can have'

[05:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'an image resolution of 2736 by 1536 or keeping on the theme of the int8 versions of models, we\'ve got the seed VR2 int8 model and a VAE for a four'

[05:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'times upscale. This goes via a one-step case sampler pass, so it\'s nice and quick, which means you can get an image which is all the way up at 5472 by 3072. Like it. That\'s far above and beyond'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what Quinn image edit can produce natively. Of course, if you do want to change a few details, then those refiners are ideal. I\'ve done a double refiner pass with the crea 2 int8 model'

[06:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to give a result that starts off at 1704 by 960. There we can see there\'s only a slight change, but that\'s because the denoise level is quite low. There\'s some'

[06:27] [scene:result]
VISUAL: AI-generated black and white comic art style image of a man
AUDIO: 'little changes there to his boot laces and some extra definition around the eyes. For the second refiner pass, the image is now 2128 by 1200 and I increased the denoise level so that things changed a'

[06:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bit more. Personally, I really like this result because rather than those smooth curved lines, it now has a straighter, more comic art style. In becoming less'

[06:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'perfect, I think it\'s become better. The point being you can use these models, whichever ones you like, to get the results that you prefer. And of course, if you wanted to then upscale this using'

[07:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seed VR to four times the result, then you totally could. If you like editing images, then as an alternative to Quinn, there\'s also Booqoo Edit for which I\'m also using the very very fast turbo int8'

[07:21] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: "Ksampler" section with nodes for model, noise, CFG Guider, Detail Daemon, Sampler/CustomAdvanced
AUDIO: 'model. I want to add something to an image in a specific place, so I\'m using a masked image. You can see my perfectly drawn manual mask covers a section of'

[07:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the fiery hair in this image with the prompt being insert a smiling rodent face in her hair. With Boogu image edit turbo, you can get away with just four steps. So, this really is very fast,'

[07:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'especially when you\'ve got an int eight version of the model. The result is almost perfect. It\'s added the rodent in the required position. Nice. If you do want some smaller overall changes, then'

[08:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: "Your Text Prompt" section with a Text String (Multiline) node containing a prompt
AUDIO: 'ultimate upscale is a great choice with the result here being 2160 by 1152. Those slightly jagged rodent teeth now have a more clear definition, and we\'ve'

[08:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'got sort of better black outlines there, along with her eyes, nose, and lips also becoming a bit more defined. This gives you a whole range of upscale options for an otherwise lower-resolution turbo edit'

[08:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model. You may also simply want to compare each of the models on the same prompt to see how well they do at something like text-to-image task, which is what I\'ve done here. The initial'

[08:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'switch to start with is the first option, the int eight clear two model, and my test prompt is a photo of a moon rodent building a massive intergalactic spaceship using carrots and some hollow'

[08:55] [scene:result]
VISUAL: AI-generated image of a rodent on a carrot-laden spaceship, demonstrating text-to-image capabilities of different models
AUDIO: 'turnips. And with that int eight clear two model, we\'ve got a result. Moon rodent building a spaceship achieved, and with a photographic style to boot. Flip a switch, and you can get the'

[09:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'result from Quen, which is more of a comic art style, and the ship has a lot of metal, and of course, it\'s very bright, but that\'s what Quen does. Flip the switch again, and you can see what Z image turbo does. We\'ve got a bright'

[09:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'blue moon sky, but the style is crisp and clear. We seem to be missing perhaps a few turnips, and the rodent\'s fur is a little bit strange, but hey, that\'s what Z image looks like. Boogu also goes for'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the comic illustration style, like Kwen did, but at least we\'ve got a couple of hollow turnips this time. Okay, let\'s get nerdy with the workflow details. Model loading is where you can select'

[09:45] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: VAE loading section, showing separate VAEs for Qwen/Krea-2 (`qwen_image_vae.safetensors`) and Z-Image/Boogu (`ae.safetensors`)
AUDIO: 'which models you\'d like to test. I\'ve gone for the int eight models because why would you not? And you could, if you wanted to, load up the FP8s or anything else that Comfy supports. Creater 2 Turbo is the first one, Kwen Image Edit'

[09:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is the second loader group with Z Image Turbo as the third and Boogoo as the fourth. Each of those models sort of shares a VAE, so I\'ve put those in separate groups as well. The Kwen Image'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and Creater one uses the Kwen Image VAE and the VAE for Z Image and Boogoo is the sort of flux AE.safetensors. Very easy to change and of course you can put whatever models you fancy there.'

[10:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Nothing difficult at all so far. The model switching is where I had most of the fun for this one as each model has slightly different requirements. This model choice group is much the same as'

[10:38] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: Conditioning section, showing `TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus` and `KREA-2 Rebalance with multiplier` nodes
AUDIO: 'in my previous video on how to easily switch models for refiner, so do check out that one for more details, but as we\'re doing the models at the beginning, uh I kind of needed to do a few extra'

[10:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'things and the way outputs the label was very useful. The real fun happens up here because whilst Kwen and Creater can happily share the text encode Kwen Image Edit Plus node, Boogoo and Z Image don\'t'

[11:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'really play very well with that, so they needed their own. Boogoo conditioning has its own text encode Boogoo Edit node with Z Image simply using the plain old clip text encode. Because everything is'

[11:20] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: Lenient Switch node in action, controlled by `Compare Text` node for model-specific conditioning
AUDIO: 'live, so to speak, the typical any switch solution would mean disabling the various groups, which which certainly one valid way to go, although instead I went with the Boolean option. Using the'

[11:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'labeled text along with Comfy\'s compare text node gives us just what is needed. A Boolean true or false option to control the switching mechanism. Does'

[11:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the option you selected have the label Boo Goo edit? If so, then use option A. Maybe instead the labeled text is Z image, in which case it\'s option B.'

[11:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If it\'s neither of those, then the default Quen conditioning can be used. Should you need more time to look and understand, now is a great time to pause before we move on.'

[12:10] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: Refiner 1 Ksampler section, showing image of an anime girl on a mug in a kitchen
AUDIO: 'The any switch method used here has multiple groups where only the active node providing any data is the one that gets through in order of precedence. This layout makes for a simpler switch,'

[12:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but then you do need to manage which groups are enabled or disabled for each model\'s companion clip and VAE nodes. Plus, you wouldn\'t know later on which choice of model you made to start with.'

[12:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That information can come in handy at the refiner stages. Here, I\'ve deliberately put the denoise steps quite high to make the image change more in this first refiner. How did we get here?'

[12:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Well, first of all I started using option D there, Boo Goo edit, along with passing in this face image. The prompt has an editing instruction, "Put her face on a mug which is on a table in an'

[13:00] [scene:result]
VISUAL: AI-generated image of an anime girl on a mug in a kitchen, after refining
AUDIO: 'ancient kitchen." With the initial result being absolutely fine, but I did want to do some refining. For the first refiner, I went with CreAi 2 because I like it. Plus, just for extra giggles'

[13:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve also enabled the re-prompting AI to describe the image. So, there you can see in the preview text, that\'s what it\'s using instead of the edit instruction which I gave in my initial'

[13:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompt. We can see the difference from that first refiner as I move the slider across. Now, I don\'t mind the background changing so much. That\'s kind of what I want, but the real issue is the face is'

[13:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'now a little bit different. This is where the memory of the first model chosen comes in handy because for the second refiner, I\'ve chosen to use'

[13:50] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI node search for "Switch", showing various switch nodes including "Lenient Switch"
AUDIO: 'BooBoo image edit again. If we zoom in take a look at the conditioning switch there, you got the lenient switch on the right. You can see there are two sets of conditioning going in. The first one'

[14:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there uses the reprompting text and a standard clip text encoder, but just underneath, we also have the original conditioning connected to source B. If you wanted manual control, you could'

[14:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'replace the lenient switch with a manual switch. The first option in the list there is the native one from ComfyUI. Click on that, we\'ve got the new node. There you can see on false, on true. So, if you'

[14:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wanted to connect that one into there, that\'s fine. I\'ll have that one. That one into there, and then you can use the output. So, you could manually switch and say, "Okay, which conditioning do I want to use?" But of course,'

[14:41] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow detail: Lenient Switch connected to `CLIP Text Encode` and `Compare Text` nodes for conditional logic
AUDIO: 'then you have to manually switch things each time and you have to remember to do that. It\'s a valid design choice, but I wanted an automatic option. That automatic option is handled by the compare text node. So, you see we have'

[14:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the initial label and the one from the second refiner. And if they end with edit, so either the Qwen edits or the BooBoo edit, then it will go, "Oh, okay." There\'s a There\'s a not gate in'

[15:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there as well. So, that\'s inverting the logic so we can say if it\'s an edit model, then option A fails. So, you\'re going to use source B. So, if you are using either Qwen image edit or BooBoo'

[15:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Edit, it will use the original conditioning. You can pause now if you want to examine the switch logic a bit more. Comparing shows the background has still changed from the original, but look at that on'

[15:33] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI workflow overview, showing the entire complex workflow with many interconnected groups and nodes
AUDIO: 'the second refiner pass, the face has been restored to the original image we started with because we\'re using the original conditioning thanks to that edit model. If we look at the original'

[15:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'versus the second refiner version, you can clearly see how the background changes, but we still retain the face similarity. Hopefully today you\'ve learned how cool'

